  "notes": "Oakland's 90s-revivalist party rap: g-funk and new-jack harmony rebuilt at the modern club spine, 90–105 straight 2&4. Three things separate it from the Mustard template it inherits. ⚠ **The bass is not an 808.** The research says \"synth bass playing a syncopated funk line rather than a kick-locked 808 — melodic, wide intervals, register E1–G2, no trap glides\", so `drums.bass808.role` moves off `bassline` to `counter_riff` and the real `bassline` part runs: `independent_riff`, `followRootsProb` 0.5, `glideProb` 0.06 for the stated absence of glides, and `anticipationProb` 0.3 for the syncopation. Register is the researched E1–G2 (28–43) exactly. ⚠ **The voicings are major-leaning over minor bass** — \"add9, maj7 keys over minor bass\" — so `major` joins the scale set the genre narrows to minor colours, `extensions` drops the triad share to 0.4, and `I–vi–IV–V` sits alongside `i–VII–VI–VII` because the research names both families. ⚠ **The tambourine on the 8ths is the 90s-revival tell**, so `tambourineMirrorsClap` is turned off — it is its own 8th-note lane, not a clap double — and `percs.lanes` carries shaker and tambourine over the genre's cowbell/triangle. ⚠ `confidence` is `medium` because the research rates this medium-high: the tempo/key cluster and the instrument list are sourced, but **`chords.extensions` and `susSubstitutionProb` are the INFERRED parameters** — \"add9, maj7\" is a colour description, not a measured distribution, and the numbers here are a reading of it. Fill fingerprint band G: `fills` 4/4, a 32nd `strong_weak_weak_weak` roll, hat rolls at 0.52 per bar; `pitchWalk` is inherited because nothing in the research says how these producers pitch a roll. ⚠ **`lockTo808` raised from 0.5 to 0.61.** The 808 takes each kick with this probability, and at 0.5 over this model's 8-kick floor a seed could produce no 808 at all — which `bass808.rs` refuses, because a declared 808 that sometimes vanishes is a part a producer cannot rely on. It is still well under a lock: a good share of kicks carry no sub.",
